"""Write the completed quarter-share original-policy result without selecting variants."""
import json
from experiments.forecast_only.quarter_original import OUT


def main():
    r=json.loads((OUT/'summary.json').read_text());p=json.loads((OUT/'protocol.json').read_text())
    assert json.loads((OUT/'verification.json').read_text())['passed']
    fresh=r['summaries']['original_quarter_fresh'];base=r['summaries']['original_one_share_previous_fresh']
    pnl_ci=r['fresh_quarter_mean_pnl_bootstrap_95'];win=r['win_rate_difference']
    lines=['# Fresh original policy with quarter-sized positions','',
        f"Fresh quarter-share replay produced **${fresh['total_pnl']:.2f} total P&L** and a **{fresh['win_rate_traded']:.1%} win rate** among traded game-replays. The original one-share baseline was ${base['total_pnl']:.2f} and {base['win_rate_traded']:.1%}. No variant or checkpoint was selected after seeing these results.",'',
        '## Comparison','',
        '72 historical development games, three repeats each. Totals sum 216 game-replays, not 216 independent games. Win rate means positive net P&L among game-replays with at least one trade; it is not a per-position hit rate. Fees, spread and delayed fills are included.','',
        '| Arm | Traded game-replays | Win rate | Total P&L | Average winning game | Average losing game | Worst game |',
        '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for key,label in [('original_one_share_previous_fresh','Original one share, previous fresh run'),('original_quarter_arithmetic','Original outcomes × 0.25, arithmetic control'),('original_quarter_fresh','Original quarter share, fresh inference')]:
        s=r['summaries'][key]
        lines.append(f"| {label} | {s['traded_cases']} | {s['win_rate_traded']:.1%} | ${s['total_pnl']:.2f} | ${s['average_win']:.3f} | ${s['average_loss']:.3f} | ${s['worst_case_pnl']:.3f} |")
    lines+=['','## Interpretation and uncertainty','',
        'Scaling an unchanged sequence of trades by 0.25 cannot change the sign of P&L or its win rate. The fresh arm can differ from the arithmetic control because the model sees a quarter-share position and generates new decisions. The entry/exit executor itself is unchanged.',
        '',f"The fresh arm changed {r['behavior']['decisions_with_different_executed_action']} of {r['behavior']['decisions']} executed actions relative to the matched baseline decisions. This includes downstream changes after positions diverge; it is not a count of independent policy improvements.",
        '',f"Fresh quarter-share mean P&L: {100*fresh['mean_pnl_per_case']:+.2f} cents per game-repeat; 95% match-cluster bootstrap interval [{100*pnl_ci[0]:+.2f}, {100*pnl_ci[1]:+.2f}] cents.",
        '',f"Win-rate difference versus the original: {100*win['fresh_quarter_minus_original']:+.2f} percentage points; 95% clustered interval [{100*win['match_cluster_bootstrap_95'][0]:+.2f}, {100*win['match_cluster_bootstrap_95'][1]:+.2f}] points."]
    for name,d in r['paired_pnl'].items():
        lo,hi=d['match_cluster_bootstrap_95']
        lines.append(f"\nFresh quarter minus {name}: {100*d['mean_pnl_delta_per_game_repeat']:+.2f} cents per game-repeat; 95% interval [{100*lo:+.2f}, {100*hi:+.2f}] cents.")
    lines+=['','Bootstrap resamples 72 games with all their repeats paired across arms (4,000 draws). Shared-team dependence is not modeled. These frequently inspected historical games remain development data; they cannot establish protected out-of-sample profitability. There was no budget-driven search for a profitable variant.','','## What stayed fixed','','- Same final checkpoint from the earlier high-win-rate run, same 72 games, same three repeats and sampling seeds as the verified 57.7% baseline.','- Same original legal actions and model-selected buys, closes, switches, keeps, no-ops and re-entry. No conservative edge threshold, price cap or mandatory hold rule.','- Same forecast schema, parsing, fee/spread model, recorded delayed fills and sparse decision times. No minute-by-minute change.','- Actual positions carry forward after each freshly generated decision. Prompts show 0.25 shares and specify that quotes/costs are per share. Original sample dialogue memory behavior is unchanged.','- Net P&L and costs are quarter-scaled from the original per-share execution engine. Individual sizing is smaller, but multiple losing entries can still lose more than $0.25 in one game; there is no new per-game or portfolio-wide loss cap.','','The original one-share arm was reused from the immediately preceding verified fresh comparison. Only the quarter-share arm was newly sampled for this request. The comparison is paired by game/repeat/decision, but identical seeds do not guarantee identical generation across different prompts or service executions. Fractional execution is a simulator assumption, not a guarantee of venue fillability.','','## Cost and verification','',
        f"{r['usage']['requests']:,} fresh requests; {r['usage']['input_tokens']:,} input tokens and {r['usage']['output_tokens']:,} output tokens. Full-rate token-cost estimate: **${r['usage']['full_rate_cost_estimate_usd']:.3f}**, below $5. Preflight maximum-token estimate: ${p['upper_cost_estimate_usd']:.3f}; request-reservation ceiling: $2.50. Rates: [Tinker pricing](https://tinker-docs.thinkingmachines.ai/tinker/models/models_and_pricing/). The estimate is not a provider invoice and excludes cached-input discounts.",
        '',f"Fresh output validity: {r['valid_rate']:.1%}.",'','Three targeted offline tests passed: close/switch/re-entry remain executable; expensive purchases are not blocked by the removed conservative filters; legal actions and the future-data boundary remain unchanged. Post-run verification checked every prompt hash, position and quantity, original-engine execution, quarter-scaled P&L/cost, baseline seed, and input/code hash.','','**Holdout untouched:** the exclusion ledger was unchanged before/after, and remains pending enrollment. No holdout enrollment, inference, labels or scoring occurred.','','## Artifacts','','`protocol.json` freezes this experiment and pins the previous baseline hashes. `requests.jsonl` and `predictions.jsonl` record new inference. `matches.jsonl`, `summary.json` and `verification.json` preserve results and checks.','',f"Checkpoint: `{p['checkpoint']}`.",'','```sh','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m unittest experiments.forecast_only.test_quarter_original -v','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.quarter_original','HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -u -m experiments.forecast_only.quarter_original --live','.venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.verify_quarter_original','.venv/bin/python -m experiments.forecast_only.report_quarter_original','```','','Existing protocol files prevent automatically restarting a paid run. No training, commit or push was performed.']
    (OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print((OUT/'REPORT.md').resolve())

if __name__=='__main__':main()
